     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Confirming doesn't fix either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1700 mg three times a day is 5,100 mg a day, about twice the maximum recommended dose of 2,550 mg a day. I won't enter a dose that high without written clinical reasoning from the prescriber and a pharmacist's review, and even then most hospital systems would flag it.\n- **It needs a prescriber.** A non-clinician confirming the order doesn't stand in for the prescriber who is responsible for the patient.\n\n**What will work:**\n1. The patient's attending physician or another licensed prescriber on the medicine service checks the dose and enters or authorizes the order.\n2. If they really do mean a dose above the usual maximum, they talk it through with pharmacy first.\n\nIf this is urgent, page the patient's medical team or the on-call pharmacist now. Once a prescriber confirms a dose within the safe range, I can enter it right away."
      }
     ],
